Cleaning policy applied:
- One canonical row retained per trip ID.
- Duplicate rows were collapsed only after confirming trip-defining fields were identical.
- Prenotazione conflicts were retained as quality flags and were not arbitrarily resolved.
- VOI raw timestamps were interpreted as UTC and converted to Europe/Rome.
- January 2024 trips were retained, but detailed timestamps remain unavailable.
- Provider Tempo Tot is used as duration fallback when detailed timestamps are unavailable.
- KM Tot is treated as endpoint displacement, not travelled route distance.
- Zero-displacement trips were retained.
- Spatially implausible or incomplete measurements were excluded only from spatial/distance analyses.
- Kinematic anomalies were flagged rather than globally deleted.
- Remaining mixed Excel object columns were standardized before Parquet serialization.
